I've redone the lost fix: all three --allow-dir symlink escapes are now refused, and the full gate passes. It's committed as 4b3fb405, on top of the WIP checkpoint d9dc4ae9. I made that checkpoint as soon as the config:: tests went green and before the long gate, so a provider failure couldn't erase the work a second time.

The bug: when canonicalize couldn't resolve a path, resolve_path fell back to the nearest existing parent directory and handled .. as plain text. That let three paths through:
1. **Dangling link:** R/link -> O/does-not-exist was judged as R/link, but writing to it creates a file in O.
2. **Link then `..:** R/link/../x, where the ..` cancelled the link on paper, but the OS follows the link first and lands in O.
3. **Link loop:** R/a <-> R/b was judged as R/a.

The fix: a new resolver, resolve_physical, now does the fallback. It walks the path one component at a time the way the OS does:
• each existing symlink is replaced by its target, and a dangling link is judged by where it points;
• .. only steps back through the part of the path that has already been resolved;
• it gives up after 40 link hops.

check_path refuses any path that can't be resolved. Paths that canonicalize already handled get the same verdict as before. The same resolver also serves the deny list, and there the change only makes it stricter.

Tests:
• **Before the fix:** five tests failed by name on unchanged code: `escape_dangling_link_out_of_root_is_refused`, `escape_link_then_parent_dir_is_refused`, `escape_link_loop_is_refused, escape_self_loop_is_refused and deny_arm_judges_the_link_target_too`.
• **Still allowed:** cases (a) to (d) from the task, plus a relative in-root link, plus a dangling link whose target is inside R. All passed before the fix and still pass.
• **Positive control:** I turned off link-following and reran the tests, then restored the file, all in one command. The escape tests failed again, and the restore left no diff and 10 of 10 passing.

Things that differ from the task file:
• **New file:** `src/config.rs` was already at its size limit (4650 lines), so the resolver and its tests went into `src/config_resolve.rs`, pulled in from `config.rs. config.rs shrank to 4640 lines, and I updated its entry in tests/module_size.rs` to match.
• **Wider match for allow and deny entries:** a configured entry that is a dangling link now resolves to its target. That could newly allow paths at the target that were refused before. I judged this acceptable because the user named that link. It isn't covered by a test, and I didn't record it in ARCHITECTURE.md either.
• **ARCHITECTURE.md:** the new bullet states the guarantee as a rule: if the filesystem doesn't change between the check and the use, no path that resolves outside every allowed directory passes check_path. It also says this doesn't protect against a link being created or changed after the check.
• Docs: I didn't change any. A grep of the two pages for "symlink" found nothing.

#996 is still open, as the task asked; the yoagent bump is Task 2.
